From: Thomas Yau <thomas.yau@kape.com>
Subject: [PATCH] chacha_asm.asm: zero-extend mLen in the small ChaCha20-Poly1305
 kernels

chacha20_poly1305_small_enc and chacha20_poly1305_small_dec take the message
length as a word32 in the 5th argument. On Windows x64 that argument is passed
on the stack, and the upper 32 bits of its 8-byte slot are undefined: MSVC only
writes the low dword. The MASM prologue loaded it with a 64-bit
`mov r10, QWORD PTR [rsp+104]`, so the length picked up stack garbage and the
kernels read/wrote far past the buffers (STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION on records of
64 bytes or less, depending on the caller's stack contents). The 7th argument
(aadLen) is already loaded with DWORD PTR; do the same for mLen.

Reported to wolfSSL; drop this patch once their fix is released.
---
diff --git a/wolfcrypt/src/chacha_asm.asm b/wolfcrypt/src/chacha_asm.asm
index 5cb2ce3..0c566fe 100644
--- a/wolfcrypt/src/chacha_asm.asm
+++ b/wolfcrypt/src/chacha_asm.asm
@@ -10005,7 +10005,7 @@ chacha20_poly1305_small_enc PROC
         push	rsi
         push	rbx
         push	rbp
-        mov	r10, QWORD PTR [rsp+104]
+        mov	r10d, DWORD PTR [rsp+104]
         mov	r11, QWORD PTR [rsp+112]
         sub	rsp, 360
         vmovdqu	OWORD PTR [rsp+200], xmm6
@@ -10498,7 +10498,7 @@ chacha20_poly1305_small_dec PROC
         push	rsi
         push	rbx
         push	rbp
-        mov	r10, QWORD PTR [rsp+104]
+        mov	r10d, DWORD PTR [rsp+104]
         mov	r11, QWORD PTR [rsp+112]
         sub	rsp, 328
         vmovdqu	OWORD PTR [rsp+168], xmm6
